                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_208\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix (EA-79438 - IAE: PopupHandler.installPopupHandler) reorders two statements in\nFileHistoryPanelImpl's constructor so that `myPopupActions = createPopupActions();` runs\nBEFORE `createDualView();`, instead of after it.\n\nTracing FileHistoryPanelImpl.java (originally FileHistoryPanel.java, renamed in\ncandidate_09) back through history shows that the constructor has always called\ncreateDualView() before assigning myPopupActions. For a long time this was harmless\nbecause createDualView() only registered anonymous PopupHandler subclasses whose\ninvokePopup() method referenced myPopupActions lazily (only evaluated when a popup\nwas actually triggered by the user, by which time the constructor had already finished\nand myPopupActions was set):\n\n    myDualView.getTreeView().addMouseListener(new PopupHandler() {\n      public void invokePopup(...) {\n        ... ActionManager.getInstance().createActionPopupMenu(ActionPlaces.UPDATE_POPUP, myPopupActions);\n      }\n    });\n\ncandidate_208 refactors createDualView() to use the PopupHandler.installPopupHandler(...)\nutility method instead of the anonymous listener classes:\n\n    PopupHandler.installPopupHandler(myDualView.getTreeView(), myPopupActions, ActionPlaces.UPDATE_POPUP, ActionManager.getInstance());\n    PopupHandler.installPopupHandler(myDualView.getFlatView(), myPopupActions, ActionPlaces.UPDATE_POPUP, ActionManager.getInstance());\n\nUnlike the old lazy closures, myPopupActions is now passed as an ordinary method\nargument, which is evaluated immediately when createDualView() executes. Since\ncreateDualView() still runs before myPopupActions is assigned in the constructor,\nmyPopupActions is null at this point, and PopupHandler.installPopupHandler\n(which builds an ActionPopupMenu from the group right away) throws an\nIllegalArgumentException \u2014 exactly the \"IAE: PopupHandler.installPopupHandler\" bug\ndescribed in the fix commit.\n\nConfirming evidence: candidate_208's resulting blob hash for FileHistoryPanelImpl.java\n(ecb621f08d0) is exactly the \"before\" blob hash of the fix commit itself, and\ncandidate_209 in this dataset is in fact the fix commit's own diff. This proves\ncandidate_208 is the last commit before the fix, and it is the commit that turned the\npreviously-harmless statement ordering into a live null-argument bug by switching to\neager evaluation of myPopupActions.\n"
